      "source_groundedness": 0.95,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A clean numeric encoding of the existing priority column, useful for correlating priority with resolution time. Largely redundant with an original column, but still adds modeling leverage. Values are a faithful mapping of the source."
    },
    {
      "name": "agent_avg_resolution_hours",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.65,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Highly relevant to 'why some agents have longer resolution times' -- provides a per-agent aggregate axis. Derivable from the table via grouping on assigned_to, though it inherits the questionable resolution_hours base and the '750' spike/'0' values suggest some aggregation artifacts."
    },
    {
      "name": "agent_concurrent_load",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.9,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A genuinely new explanatory axis (workload) that plausibly explains slower resolution -- strong analytical value. Computable from overlapping open intervals per agent, but this depends on opened_at/closed_at which are not visible in samples, so only partially verifiable."
    },
    {
      "name": "category_avg_resolution_hours",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.75,
      "source_groundedness": 0.7,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "Adds a category-level benchmark useful for separating agent effects from case-type effects. Derivable by grouping on the existing category column, though it inherits the resolution_hours reliability issues."
    },
    {
      "name": "is_self_closed",
      "analytical_usefulness": 0.65,
      "source_groundedness": 0.8,
      "hallucination_observed": false,
      "rationale": "A meaningful binary flag (whether closed_by equals assigned_to/caller) that could correlate with resolution behaviour. Derivable by comparing closed_by with other person fields; a reasonable categorisation, though the samples don't fully expose the compared fields."
    }
  ],
  "analytical_usefulness": 0.85,
  "source_groundedness": 0.68,
  "rationale": "The added columns are well-aimed at the query: they supply the core resolution-time metric plus multiple distinct explanatory axes (agent averages, concurrent workload, category benchmark, self-closed flag, priority encoding), giving real leverage to explain why some agents are slower. The main weakness is groundedness of resolution_hours: numerous negative values are not a sound reading of timestamps, and since resolution_hours feeds the agent/category averages, that unreliability propagates. Values are otherwise consistent with grouping/encoding of existing columns."
